1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,430
Some pages belong in two places.

2
00:00:02,513 --> 00:00:07,303
March the fourteenth belongs to March,
and it also belongs to Week 11.

3
00:00:07,422 --> 00:00:11,550
This episode is about references:
how one page lives in both,

4
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:14,371
and how to link and label across them.

5
00:00:14,582 --> 00:00:17,762
In the hierarchy, open
Weeks, then Week 11.

6
00:00:17,824 --> 00:00:21,714
Its seven rows are in italics,
with a small link icon.

7
00:00:21,793 --> 00:00:23,143
They aren't pages.

8
00:00:23,264 --> 00:00:27,685
They're references: pointers to the
real days, which live under March.

9
00:00:27,901 --> 00:00:32,288
Select one, and instead of a title
and fields there is just a card:

10
00:00:32,288 --> 00:00:34,371
this node links to March 14.

11
00:00:34,456 --> 00:00:36,696
A reference has nothing of its own.

12
00:00:36,781 --> 00:00:40,221
Anything that lands on it goes
straight through to the real day.

13
00:00:40,430 --> 00:00:42,490
Why not simply copy the days?

14
00:00:42,621 --> 00:00:44,831
Because a copy is a second page.

15
00:00:44,869 --> 00:00:47,457
Write on one, and the other never knows.

16
00:00:47,568 --> 00:00:51,278
A reference keeps one page,
reachable from two places,

17
00:00:51,278 --> 00:00:53,727
and the PDF prints it only once.

18
00:00:53,936 --> 00:00:55,536
Let's make some of our own.

19
00:00:55,590 --> 00:00:59,115
On the top page, Add New
Page, and call it Birthdays.

20
00:00:59,147 --> 00:01:02,154
It should list its pages
the way Weeks and Notes do,

21
00:01:02,154 --> 00:01:04,427
so it gets the List Index template.

22
00:01:04,566 --> 00:01:07,682
A new page borrows the first
template in the project,

23
00:01:07,682 --> 00:01:10,107
here Year View, so this step matters.

24
00:01:10,314 --> 00:01:14,226
Hover Birthdays, and the link
button, Link Existing Page,

25
00:01:14,226 --> 00:01:17,564
opens a picker: the same
tree as the sidebar.

26
00:01:17,690 --> 00:01:20,450
I'll unfold Quarter 1, and then March.

27
00:01:20,513 --> 00:01:23,985
Every day of March is in
here, each one a real page.

28
00:01:24,093 --> 00:01:27,713
I want March the fourteenth, and
clicking it makes the reference.

29
00:01:27,928 --> 00:01:29,688
One more, from the summer.

30
00:01:29,758 --> 00:01:32,408
Quarter 3, July, and July the second.

31
00:01:32,484 --> 00:01:37,072
Each pick is added at the end of the list,
so add them in the order you want them to

32
00:01:37,072 --> 00:01:37,704
appear.

33
00:01:37,806 --> 00:01:42,756
And there's no limit: a page can be
referenced from as many places as you like.

34
00:01:42,964 --> 00:01:47,843
Birthdays now lists both days, and each
one is a link to the real day page.

35
00:01:47,974 --> 00:01:52,384
In the sidebar, the new rows are
italic: references, not copies.

36
00:01:52,597 --> 00:01:55,716
To reach Birthdays from
the year page, one change:

37
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:59,397
its second list shows three
sections, starting at four.

38
00:01:59,497 --> 00:02:03,587
Make that four, and Birthdays joins
Weeks, Notes and To-Do Lists.

39
00:02:03,795 --> 00:02:08,055
From a day, the way back to its week
is a link called Go to Referrer.

40
00:02:08,129 --> 00:02:12,080
On the Day View template, the
weekday chip in the corner uses it:

41
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:16,828
find the reference that points at this
day, and go to the page it sits on.

42
00:02:17,035 --> 00:02:21,594
March 14 now has two references,
the week's and the birthday list's.

43
00:02:21,686 --> 00:02:25,963
Go to Referrer takes the first one
ever made, which is the week's,

44
00:02:25,963 --> 00:02:28,416
so this chip still means: my week.

45
00:02:28,627 --> 00:02:33,597
Month View's week numbers come from a
formula instead, called child referrer.

46
00:02:33,669 --> 00:02:38,469
It asks which page references this month's
days, and prints that page's title.

47
00:02:38,679 --> 00:02:42,334
It has four parts: which day to
start from, how many to scan,

48
00:02:42,334 --> 00:02:45,879
which kind of page to prefer,
and which field to print.

49
00:02:45,922 --> 00:02:47,782
You rarely type it by hand.

50
00:02:47,868 --> 00:02:51,818
Insert Referrer Field opens a
builder that writes it for you.

51
00:02:52,025 --> 00:02:54,375
Let's export and follow it all the way.

52
00:02:54,517 --> 00:02:57,896
It's a long document, more
than thirteen hundred pages,

53
00:02:57,896 --> 00:02:59,927
so the export takes a moment.

54
00:03:00,069 --> 00:03:05,556
It walks every page in order, skips the
references so each day prints only once,

55
00:03:05,556 --> 00:03:08,618
and writes every link as a real PDF link.

56
00:03:08,828 --> 00:03:12,215
From the year page, Birthdays,
which lists both days.

57
00:03:12,321 --> 00:03:15,015
Then March 14, the real day page.

58
00:03:15,087 --> 00:03:20,331
And the weekday chip, Sat, goes to Week
11, the page that holds its reference.

59
00:03:20,539 --> 00:03:23,702
One page, two ways in,
and a way back from each.

60
00:03:23,825 --> 00:03:27,593
Next time: variants, and one
document for every device.
